WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.992 --> 00:00:21.345
"I hope Alpha is recalibrated by now," Ally thought as she raced home from work.

2
00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:27.850
She'd just walked through the front door when her phone pinged.

3
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:33.873
Now that Alpha was inside the new computer, Ally's new phone was working great for calls and texts.

4
00:00:34.574 --> 00:00:36.214
She saw a message from Julius.

5
00:00:38.275 --> 00:00:38.776
Julius: Hi, Ally!

6
00:00:39.176 --> 00:00:42.017
My plane got delayed so I just got to Grandma's this morning.

7
00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:43.898
Ally: How is it?

8
00:00:44.258 --> 00:00:45.879
Are you having a good time so far?

9
00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:47.379
Julius: It's great.

10
00:00:47.799 --> 00:00:52.081
All of Grandma's friends watched Food Truck Rally, and they can't believe that I know the winners.

11
00:00:53.202 --> 00:00:55.183
They all said you were their favorite on the team.

12
00:00:56.123 --> 00:00:58.304
You're famous, people want to know all about you!

13
00:01:00.728 --> 00:01:00.888
"Oh no!"

14
00:01:00.908 --> 00:01:01.348
Ally thought.

15
00:01:01.368 --> 00:01:04.069
"I don't want people asking questions about me!

16
00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:09.592
Although, without my powers, no one would believe I'm an alien anyway!"

17
00:01:10.452 --> 00:01:13.753
Ally didn't want to type that, so she sent a smiley face emoji.

18
00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:16.435
Julius: How's everything back in Sandville?

19
00:01:16.455 --> 00:01:17.715
Ally: Good.

20
00:01:18.195 --> 00:01:20.256
Busy, today was Bong!

21
00:01:20.816 --> 00:01:22.537
A loud noise came from her room.

22
00:01:22.557 --> 00:01:26.219
"Alpha!" Ally ran into her room.

23
00:01:26.239 --> 00:01:28.660
Ally: Can I text you later?

24
00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.897
Alpha She quickly deleted the word.

25
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.880
Ally: My new computer just booted up!

26
00:01:38.743 --> 00:01:42.727
Just then Ally heard another sound—the sweetest one ever.

27
00:01:42.747 --> 00:01:51.775
"Greetings. I am Alpha CXB unit serial number 7638hbc81 at your service."

28
00:01:51.795 --> 00:01:53.837
"You're back, Alpha!

29
00:01:54.337 --> 00:01:55.638
Are you fully functional?"

30
00:01:56.179 --> 00:01:57.360
Ally crossed her fingers.

31
00:01:58.288 --> 00:02:01.629
"Some memory files must still be restored," Alpha said.

32
00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:07.592
"Due to the primitive nature of this Earth technology, progress is slow, but I am ready to serve."

33
00:02:07.612 --> 00:02:10.713
"I'm so happy, I could hug you!"

34
00:02:11.433 --> 00:02:13.954
Ally rushed to throw her arms around the computer.

35
00:02:14.275 --> 00:02:15.055
Beep! Beep!

36
00:02:15.715 --> 00:02:16.816
"Halt, Allyzooba!

37
00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:21.317
That is human behavior— an inappropriate response for an Astralian!"

38
00:02:21.337 --> 00:02:23.778
"You're right."

39
00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:25.299
Ally hung her head.

40
00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:27.220
"I don't want to be human.

41
00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:32.690
I want to be an Astralian, one who makes her parents proud one day."

42
00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:36.212
"That is admirable," Alpha said.

43
00:02:36.232 --> 00:02:39.654
"My memory banks have retrieved an old request from you.

44
00:02:40.114 --> 00:02:42.175
You wanted me to help you find your powers.

45
00:02:42.956 --> 00:02:45.337
Confirm this situation has been corrected."

46
00:02:45.357 --> 00:02:47.318
"It hasn't!"

47
00:02:48.979 --> 00:02:49.639
Ally sighed.

48
00:02:49.659 --> 00:02:52.381
"I still need your help getting them back.

49
00:02:54.262 --> 00:02:57.824
It happened right after I watched the lunar eclipse at the park."

50
00:03:00.168 --> 00:03:02.090
"Issue located," Alpha said.

51
00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:04.051
"Astralia has no moon.

52
00:03:04.492 --> 00:03:07.014
Therefore, there are no lunar eclipses."

53
00:03:07.034 --> 00:03:09.956
"I know that," Ally said.

54
00:03:09.976 --> 00:03:12.258
"What does that have to do with my problem?"

55
00:03:12.278 --> 00:03:17.382
"Astralians can be affected by maladies when exposed to lunar eclipses."

56
00:03:18.423 --> 00:03:19.104
Alpha frowned.

57
00:03:19.124 --> 00:03:23.527
"This is basic information taught to young Astralians in first grade."

58
00:03:24.568 --> 00:03:25.229
Ally gulped.

59
00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.972
"I really should have paid more attention in school.

60
00:03:29.588 --> 00:03:33.050
I never would have gone outside during the eclipse if I'd known that."

61
00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:38.413
"You also would have learned how to fix the maladies in the same lesson," Alpha said.

62
00:03:38.433 --> 00:03:40.034
"What do you mean?"

63
00:03:40.494 --> 00:03:41.134
Ally asked.

64
00:03:42.075 --> 00:03:44.736
"Viewing a solar eclipse will reverse the effects.

65
00:03:45.396 --> 00:03:49.979
However, it is dangerous to view a solar eclipse without proper eye protection."

66
00:03:49.999 --> 00:03:51.660
"I'll get some!

67
00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:52.840
Whatever I need!"

68
00:03:53.201 --> 00:03:53.721
Ally said.

69
00:03:53.741 --> 00:03:56.242
"When is the next solar eclipse?"

70
00:03:57.343 --> 00:04:00.221
"Eclipses occur in pairs on Earth," Alpha said.

71
00:04:00.241 --> 00:04:04.584
"The next solar eclipse is due to occur in exactly five days."

72
00:04:04.604 --> 00:04:06.366
"Great news!"

73
00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:08.928
Ally did a little happy dance.

74
00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.290
"I knew you'd figure it out!

75
00:04:12.311 --> 00:04:14.512
I'll have my powers back by next week!"

76
00:04:15.433 --> 00:04:17.035
"Affirmative," Alpha said.

77
00:04:17.055 --> 00:04:20.017
"However, there is one—" "Argh!"

78
00:04:20.397 --> 00:04:23.060
Mateo shouted in the hallway outside Ally's door.

79
00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:28.064
Ally threw open her door and saw Mateo standing there with his tablet in his hands.

80
00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.141
"What happened, Mateo?

81
00:04:30.561 --> 00:04:31.342
Are you all right?"

82
00:04:32.322 --> 00:04:34.624
"No!" Mateo wailed.

83
00:04:34.644 --> 00:04:36.405
"Where are you hurt?

84
00:04:36.905 --> 00:04:38.166
Should I call an ambulance?"

85
00:04:38.987 --> 00:04:41.208
Mateo shook his head, looking miserable.

86
00:04:41.228 --> 00:04:45.231
"No doctor could mend my broken heart now."

87
00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:46.932
"Oh no!"

88
00:04:47.432 --> 00:04:48.033
Ally cried.

89
00:04:48.053 --> 00:04:50.214
"Did Bethany break up with you?"

90
00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:53.817
"No!" Mateo looked insulted.

91
00:04:53.837 --> 00:04:56.658
"The other bidder won the comic book.

92
00:04:57.219 --> 00:04:58.620
The auction is over."

93
00:04:59.488 --> 00:05:01.790
"I'm so sorry."

94
00:05:03.111 --> 00:05:04.772
Ally patted Mateo on the shoulder.

95
00:05:05.453 --> 00:05:06.954
"I know how much you wanted it."

96
00:05:06.974 --> 00:05:11.818
"I'll get over this one day," Mateo said, hanging his head.

97
00:05:11.838 --> 00:05:14.580
"Wait." He looked up again.

98
00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.582
"Did I hear Alpha's voice?

99
00:05:17.042 --> 00:05:17.763
Is she back?

100
00:05:18.183 --> 00:05:20.305
Did she find the answer to getting your powers back?"

101
00:05:21.426 --> 00:05:23.067
"She is and she did!"

102
00:05:23.527 --> 00:05:24.008
Ally said.

103
00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:30.223
"All I have to do is go outside during the solar eclipse in five days, and I'll have

104
00:05:30.283 --> 00:05:31.424
my powers back."

105
00:05:32.745 --> 00:05:34.666
"Awesome!" Mateo said.

106
00:05:34.686 --> 00:05:38.128
"Let's see what we can find out about that solar eclipse."

107
00:05:39.909 --> 00:05:41.190
He typed into his tablet.

108
00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:44.752
A few seconds later he hung his head again.

109
00:05:44.772 --> 00:05:49.575
"Um, Ally, I have some bad news."
